  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "2.6.0: with ChromaDotNet.Client 2.6.0, no change of its own. 2.5.0: AddChromaClient and AddKeyedChromaClient with an action that configures the IHttpClientBuilder, for a resilience handler, a proxy or a timeout; the singleton client applies the settings of its HttpClient, like ConfigureHttpClient, which were lost. 2.4.1: works in applications published with trimming or NativeAOT, with IsAotCompatible. 2.4.0: AddChromaClient and AddKeyedChromaClient register one ChromaClient singleton per key, so also singletons can take it; its HttpClient takes the current handler of IHttpClientFactory at each request, renewed after two minutes by default, on every target. 2.3.0: AddKeyedChromaClient registers a client and its options under a key. 2.0.0: AddChromaClient registers the options, which the client needs. Release notes of the client: https://github.com/ChromaDotNet/ChromaDB.Client/releases",
